{"id": "EUVD-2026-76332", "enisaUuid": "e946e45a-4b64-3ae3-836c-95439c761694", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nio_uring/query: cap user size passed to copy_struct_to_user\n\nio_handle_query_entry() clamps hdr.size for the inbound copy_from_user()\nbut keeps the original user value as usize. copy_struct_to_user() uses\nthat usize and, when it is larger than the kernel result, clear_user()s\nthe trailing bytes.\n\nAs hdr.size is a __u32, a query can request nearly 4 GiB of zeroing,\nincluding on the error path where res_size stays 0. The interface is\nreachable without a ring via IORING_REGISTER_QUERY.\n\nReject sizes larger than PAGE_SIZE, as recommended for copy_struct_*\ninterfaces.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:46:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/417e02f7b6051765b91cf1289071882eebd172e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b8ad4981ecedb14c1fdd811ab977010b23933e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba77efee1b95b4ad7559b1cdbe7cd7fa36dca95b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-81009", "GHSA-w44c-cv6c-x94c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "37315b3c-1c47-3d09-91df-86b2846572ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "68e84900-c004-3755-b2ce-4c485728ef69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "81dbde30-34ca-3d3a-86f7-d287c9792190", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c265ae75f900cea4e415230a77b5d152377627dd <2b8ad4981ecedb14c1fdd811ab977010b23933e6"}, {"id": "8246742a-e069-3785-b931-97995d945d52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c265ae75f900cea4e415230a77b5d152377627dd <ba77efee1b95b4ad7559b1cdbe7cd7fa36dca95b"}, {"id": "88a2b817-8aa1-3e4d-b455-1ab149b60e6a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "96d1df03-5a55-3751-aae4-1b3c9f270744", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c265ae75f900cea4e415230a77b5d152377627dd <417e02f7b6051765b91cf1289071882eebd172e0"}, {"id": "b250847e-d89a-3b0f-91cc-1c1876d34dda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "cdc61a9c-0882-3140-801d-b077b55bff5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1c71d965-4207-38b0-81eb-101ecd49b865", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}